    "field": "Seasonal forecasting",
    "problem": "The ECMWF System 4 seasonal forecast model develops a systematic bias causing the simulated western Pacific Intertropical Convergence Zone to drift northwards, a process which develops early in hindcasts and adversely affects the quality of the forecasts.",
    "method": "This study proposes a diagnostic approach that compares fully coupled atmosphere-ocean hindcasts with atmosphere-only hindcasts to trace the initial evolution of systematic biases and identify the atmospheric origins of the simulated Intertropical Convergence Zone drift.",
    "task": "The task is to identify the causes of the northward drift of the Western Pacific Intertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) in ECMWF System 4 hindcasts by examining the initial evolution of systematic biases in the forecast model.",
